# Code Review & Production Readiness Review (PRR) Checklist

## 1. Architectural & Code Quality Rules
- [ ] Code follows Clean Architecture (Domain isolated from infrastructure).
- [ ] SOLID principles satisfied; interfaces segregated and injected via DI.
- [ ] Pull Request is under 400 lines of diff.
- [ ] Code comments explain *why*, not obvious *what*.

## 2. Resilience & Stability
- [ ] All network and database calls have explicit timeouts.
- [ ] Retries use exponential backoff with full jitter for transient errors.
- [ ] Circuit breakers guard fragile downstream dependencies.
- [ ] Application trap `SIGTERM` and handles graceful shutdown within deadline.
- [ ] Liveness, Readiness, and Startup health checks configured.

## 3. Observability & Operations
- [ ] Logs are emitted as structured JSON with trace correlation (`trace_id`, `span_id`).
- [ ] RED & USE metrics exposed on `/metrics`.
- [ ] W3C `traceparent` context propagated on outbound RPC/HTTP.

## 4. Security & Compliance
- [ ] Zero secrets, API keys, or connection strings in source code.
- [ ] Inputs validated against typed schemas.
- [ ] Database queries executed via parameterized queries / ORM (no string concatenation SQL).
- [ ] TLS 1.3 / mTLS enforced.

## 5. Testing & Verification
- [ ] Unit test coverage >= 70%.
- [ ] Integration tests verify database migrations and infrastructure queries.
- [ ] Automated build and test pipeline passes clean.
